      "id": "ejnav8a",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Need for Classification of Elements"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Dobereiner grouped elements into Triads where the atomic mass of the middle element was approximately the arithmetic mean of the other two.",
        "Newlands arranged elements by increasing atomic mass and stated that every eighth element has similar properties (Law of Octaves).",
        "Mendeleev published the first periodic table arranging elements by atomic mass and left gaps for undiscovered elements.",
        "Henry Moseley established that atomic number, not atomic mass, is the primary property determining chemical behavior.",
        "Atomic radius decreases across a period from left to right and increases down a group, whereas electronegativity and ionization energy show the reverse trend."
      ],
      "id": "2bmkhtn"
    },
